count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T14:55:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Help Assistant infra deploy: gpt-5-mini isn''t available in centralindia (#47)\n\nPipeline run failed with InvalidResourceProperties — ''GlobalStandard'' SKU for\ngpt-4o-mini isn''t supported in centralindia. Per Microsoft''s own model/region\ntable, gpt-5-mini (which we actually want) has the same problem: centralindia\nisn''t in its GlobalStandard region list at all. southindia is the closest\nregion that does support it, so:\n\n- ai-foundry.bicep: default chatModelName/chatModelVersion -> gpt-5-mini /\n  2025-08-07, with a comment listing the supported regions and flagging that\n  gpt-5-family models may need subscription registration\n- infra-help-assistant.yml / deploy-ai-foundry.sh: default LOCATION ->\n  southindia for this Foundry-specific infra only — deliberately independent\n  of the AKS cluster''s centralindia (main.bicep), since Foundry/AI\n  Search/Storage don''t need to be co-located with AKS for this workload\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f0a49cd50e24ff4275c2ca08f9ce738d5cb7840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/2f0a49cd50e24ff4275c2ca08f9ce738d5cb7840"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/f2494518f3c154ec5f0009e05ab26ba3c22d1f12","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f0a49cd50e24ff4275c2ca08f9ce738d5cb7840\nparent bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8\nauthor ankitgoelmalviyans <157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com> 1784904924 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784904924 +0530\n\nFix Help Assistant infra deploy: gpt-5-mini isn''t available in centralindia (#47)\n\nPipeline run failed with InvalidResourceProperties — ''GlobalStandard'' SKU for\ngpt-4o-mini isn''t supported in centralindia. Per Microsoft''s own model/region\ntable, gpt-5-mini (which we actually want) has the same problem: centralindia\nisn''t in its GlobalStandard region list at all. southindia is the closest\nregion that does support it, so:\n\n- ai-foundry.bicep: default chatModelName/chatModelVersion -> gpt-5-mini /\n  2025-08-07, with a comment listing the supported regions and flagging that\n  gpt-5-family models may need subscription registration\n- infra-help-assistant.yml / deploy-ai-foundry.sh: default LOCATION ->\n  southindia for this Foundry-specific infra only — deliberately independent\n  of the AKS cluster''s centralindia (main.bicep), since Foundry/AI\n  Search/Storage don''t need to be co-located with AKS for this workload\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY3zcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5fQQAJnlCKIkF9u4sZeVMZHVitzw\nn7VzC3E8Qa9TsQw4FFZJA6jnE88L3AsmrolwKdVmfw1m0BROATKGkbYyEkq/02am\nXmMsJGYHCTLJs/LhC9ow8Fqt/N7xBT4LObFXHdT1RdKchGE7e8149W3UkoTHtaRl\nfrUObElMTC+moJBgmBwVfYmAySEks87O38IvT/hoaCeVx+K1SRS1Xqz4m05zINdw\nL5nQ/WJUMtEnoRe9ofaZSGpU4QlfFAOtqpUO7kj8YJv3hlyp63F71fO/L5LBiR9n\nk9kSfRTTunDz/YDBqp5CVDiLdzp0SklUULJHX/sR1nZ8N/a7FH++wA3O1xdnTOqC\nBH8Ato4W6Hcen3bRBYhVdXjnnsTs4/UtxzLx/u8dYK/lRyj7wJiyOtwRAxKt1QoS\nvNRgXVGjkbACm/AiuB4NRllVrCoQflZxVcVc1ZnWvTzuzFl3n+HgMOUq0Lza6nBz\nfdj+Tok58CzN4LccTsa2bJv6A3iHUa2OPHXXlIfKof0aYB72YTeLviUnfpZijUNV\nKzoOum6s8dr/YLOfOx5fcKAX3Cybm87UQ/czsZfM9n39KWCnckhpDWhDEw8EBM+i\nPjPfK+3H+bm5KPLY1ZSw7frsQXQ1Uy5EGGiN0mM/PFnYFGq63zn3I+2qJ8oB6wIE\nFFWFLow6SsV8ltpMjJZY\n=KE6r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-24T14:55:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/f2494518f3c154ec5f0009e05ab26ba3c22d1f12","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKGYyNDk0NTE4ZjNjMTU0ZWM1ZjAwMDllMDVhYjI2YmEzYzIyZDFmMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8","sha":"bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8"}],"sha":"f2494518f3c154ec5f0009e05ab26ba3c22d1f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/f2494518f3c154ec5f0009e05ab26ba3c22d1f12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T14:41:59Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T14:41:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Claude/project remaining work m5h0ek (#46)\n\n* Added Support of Cosmos vector-search capability\n\n* fix: Coderabbit suggestion\n\n* feat: train a real matrix-factorization model for co-purchase recommendations\n\nRecommendationService''s \"customers who bought X also bought Y\" was pure raw\nco-occurrence counting with no training step. Add a genuine trained tier: a\none-class matrix-factorization model (ML.NET) over captured order baskets\n(OrderId x ProductId), with per-product latent vectors ranked by cosine\nsimilarity into a new ProductSimilarityModel container.\n\n- New OrderBaskets container captures raw per-order basket data as durable\n  training input (RecommendationService.RecordOrderAsync), independent of the\n  existing pairwise-count writes.\n- CoPurchaseModelTrainer trains the model as a pure function over domain\n  types; RecommendationModelTrainingWorker retrains it periodically, gated by\n  its own Recommendations:ModelTrainingEnabled flag.\n- GetRecommendationsAsync prefers the trained model per-product, falling back\n  to the original raw-count logic for any product without model coverage yet\n  (new products, thin data, training disabled) — existing behavior and tests\n  are unchanged when no model record exists.\n- Provision the two new Cosmos containers (bicep), bump RecommendationService''s\n  Helm resources for ML.NET''s runtime footprint, and add the new CI secret.\n- Add scripts/ReplaySeedOrders, a one-off tool to backfill training data from\n  the 75 existing seed orders (which predate basket capture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix:CodeRabbitSuggestions\n\n* fix: coderabbit -  backfill baskets directly via Cosmos, dropping the Service Bus replay path entirely.\n\n* AzureFoundry Support for help file RAG operations\n\n* Fix: New Help Agent\n\n* Move Help Assistant infra deploy/index/publish steps into a pipeline\n\ndeploy-ai-foundry.sh, setup-ai-search-pipeline.sh, and\ndeploy-foundry-agent-publish.sh are now driven by a new\ninfra-help-assistant.yml workflow (deploy-base-infra + setup-search-pipeline\non push, publish-agent via workflow_dispatch) rather than run by hand, matching\nthe existing infra-bicep.yml convention.\n\nAgent creation itself moves fully to the Foundry portal (Agents panel) — drop\nsetup-foundry-agent.sh''s REST-based agent creation entirely in favor of\ncreate-help-assistant-service-principal.sh, which only creates the Entra ID\napp registration (a Graph/directory operation AZURE_CREDENTIALS can''t and\nshouldn''t be granted rights for). deploy-foundry-agent-publish.sh now takes\nagentName/agentVersion/applicationName as arguments so it can publish whatever\nwas created manually.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review findings on PR #46\n\n- sync-help-docs.yml: add permissions: contents: read, persist-credentials:\n  false, a concurrency group (concurrent runs with --delete-destination true\n  can otherwise delete/overwrite blobs mid-sync), and rename the job label\n  (it syncs Markdown, not PDFs)\n- infra-help-assistant.yml: add permissions: contents: read; fix a script-\n  injection vector where workflow_dispatch inputs were spliced directly into\n  run: shell blocks — route them through env: and reference as $VAR instead,\n  since raw ${{ }} expansion happens before the shell parses the script\n- HelpAssistantController: reject messages with blank content or an\n  unsupported role (400) instead of silently coercing them into a user turn\n- Dockerfile: run the runtime container as the built-in non-root `app` user\n- Program.cs/HelpAssistantController: rate-limit the anonymous /ask endpoint\n  (10 req/min per client IP) — it proxies to a paid model with no auth signal\n  other than IP to partition on\n- FoundryAgentClient: stop logging the raw Foundry error response body on\n  failure (could echo prompt/generated content from an anonymous endpoint) —\n  log status code only\n- HelpAssistantChatServiceTests: strengthen truncation assertions to check\n  actual retained content/slice, not just count and last-element\n- ai-foundry.bicep: add explicit dependsOn between the two sibling model\n  deployments — ARM deploys them in parallel by default, and Cognitive\n  Services accounts only allow one write at a time on the parent, causing an\n  intermittent RequestConflict\n\nNot applied, with reasons:\n- CodeQL log-injection findings on ExceptionMiddleware/RequestLoggingMiddleware\n  logging Request.Path — identical to the pattern already used unmodified by\n  every other service in this repo; fixing only this copy doesn''t address the\n  systemic (pre-existing, out-of-scope) pattern, and Serilog''s JSON formatter\n  limits actual injection risk versus plain-text logs\n- Restricting the fake Foundry client to Development and failing startup\n  otherwise — deliberately contradicts this repo''s established\n  \"deploys unconditionally, degrades to a fake client when credentials are\n  unset regardless of environment\" posture, identical to AiService and\n  PaymentService\n- foundryApiKey browser exposure / missing AbortController in\n  help-assistant.component.ts — both stale, the direct-SPA-to-Foundry design\n  they referred to was already replaced by the HelpAssistantService backend\n  proxy in an earlier commit on this branch\n- deploy-ai-foundry.sh missing set -euo pipefail / unquoted args — both\n  already fixed in an earlier commit\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c7414e076daed1e13e9fb6f73bc69910b4a1c2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/0c7414e076daed1e13e9fb6f73bc69910b4a1c2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c7414e076daed1e13e9fb6f73bc69910b4a1c2a\nparent 8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6\nauthor ankitgoelmalviyans <157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com> 1784904119 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784904119 +0530\n\nClaude/project remaining work m5h0ek (#46)\n\n* Added Support of Cosmos vector-search capability\n\n* fix: Coderabbit suggestion\n\n* feat: train a real matrix-factorization model for co-purchase recommendations\n\nRecommendationService''s \"customers who bought X also bought Y\" was pure raw\nco-occurrence counting with no training step. Add a genuine trained tier: a\none-class matrix-factorization model (ML.NET) over captured order baskets\n(OrderId x ProductId), with per-product latent vectors ranked by cosine\nsimilarity into a new ProductSimilarityModel container.\n\n- New OrderBaskets container captures raw per-order basket data as durable\n  training input (RecommendationService.RecordOrderAsync), independent of the\n  existing pairwise-count writes.\n- CoPurchaseModelTrainer trains the model as a pure function over domain\n  types; RecommendationModelTrainingWorker retrains it periodically, gated by\n  its own Recommendations:ModelTrainingEnabled flag.\n- GetRecommendationsAsync prefers the trained model per-product, falling back\n  to the original raw-count logic for any product without model coverage yet\n  (new products, thin data, training disabled) — existing behavior and tests\n  are unchanged when no model record exists.\n- Provision the two new Cosmos containers (bicep), bump RecommendationService''s\n  Helm resources for ML.NET''s runtime footprint, and add the new CI secret.\n- Add scripts/ReplaySeedOrders, a one-off tool to backfill training data from\n  the 75 existing seed orders (which predate basket capture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix:CodeRabbitSuggestions\n\n* fix: coderabbit -  backfill baskets directly via Cosmos, dropping the Service Bus replay path entirely.\n\n* AzureFoundry Support for help file RAG operations\n\n* Fix: New Help Agent\n\n* Move Help Assistant infra deploy/index/publish steps into a pipeline\n\ndeploy-ai-foundry.sh, setup-ai-search-pipeline.sh, and\ndeploy-foundry-agent-publish.sh are now driven by a new\ninfra-help-assistant.yml workflow (deploy-base-infra + setup-search-pipeline\non push, publish-agent via workflow_dispatch) rather than run by hand, matching\nthe existing infra-bicep.yml convention.\n\nAgent creation itself moves fully to the Foundry portal (Agents panel) — drop\nsetup-foundry-agent.sh''s REST-based agent creation entirely in favor of\ncreate-help-assistant-service-principal.sh, which only creates the Entra ID\napp registration (a Graph/directory operation AZURE_CREDENTIALS can''t and\nshouldn''t be granted rights for). deploy-foundry-agent-publish.sh now takes\nagentName/agentVersion/applicationName as arguments so it can publish whatever\nwas created manually.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review findings on PR #46\n\n- sync-help-docs.yml: add permissions: contents: read, persist-credentials:\n  false, a concurrency group (concurrent runs with --delete-destination true\n  can otherwise delete/overwrite blobs mid-sync), and rename the job label\n  (it syncs Markdown, not PDFs)\n- infra-help-assistant.yml: add permissions: contents: read; fix a script-\n  injection vector where workflow_dispatch inputs were spliced directly into\n  run: shell blocks — route them through env: and reference as $VAR instead,\n  since raw ${{ }} expansion happens before the shell parses the script\n- HelpAssistantController: reject messages with blank content or an\n  unsupported role (400) instead of silently coercing them into a user turn\n- Dockerfile: run the runtime container as the built-in non-root `app` user\n- Program.cs/HelpAssistantController: rate-limit the anonymous /ask endpoint\n  (10 req/min per client IP) — it proxies to a paid model with no auth signal\n  other than IP to partition on\n- FoundryAgentClient: stop logging the raw Foundry error response body on\n  failure (could echo prompt/generated content from an anonymous endpoint) —\n  log status code only\n- HelpAssistantChatServiceTests: strengthen truncation assertions to check\n  actual retained content/slice, not just count and last-element\n- ai-foundry.bicep: add explicit dependsOn between the two sibling model\n  deployments — ARM deploys them in parallel by default, and Cognitive\n  Services accounts only allow one write at a time on the parent, causing an\n  intermittent RequestConflict\n\nNot applied, with reasons:\n- CodeQL log-injection findings on ExceptionMiddleware/RequestLoggingMiddleware\n  logging Request.Path — identical to the pattern already used unmodified by\n  every other service in this repo; fixing only this copy doesn''t address the\n  systemic (pre-existing, out-of-scope) pattern, and Serilog''s JSON formatter\n  limits actual injection risk versus plain-text logs\n- Restricting the fake Foundry client to Development and failing startup\n  otherwise — deliberately contradicts this repo''s established\n  \"deploys unconditionally, degrades to a fake client when credentials are\n  unset regardless of environment\" posture, identical to AiService and\n  PaymentService\n- foundryApiKey browser exposure / missing AbortController in\n  help-assistant.component.ts — both stale, the direct-SPA-to-Foundry design\n  they referred to was already replaced by the HelpAssistantService backend\n  proxy in an earlier commit on this branch\n- deploy-ai-foundry.sh missing set -euo pipefail / unquoted args — both\n  already fixed in an earlier commit\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqY3m3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwvwQAIoD39kQHZmANqAEb8tz2gVR\nB9bWUMXslwsCf3Dkt/6P17U5XrX6JRliOpkHxUaM4agUVppQw7LuzJy+YaOpptY1\nBDVFpQ2MPD0iasP4aGI1jQSMLSWBnQNvkfYPJgZg/5xePRBb/lHY5i9ZsvR0Ai+s\nuUa0Mxj5EXC0FyQt6ASYtS4aVNlQ9EtuXjx6aNChX4VW4KpEKBgmsVfspRmUOVUc\nmaJ4ZOjUCIYxf+m+IE9MXaMEMmeh3bdMmh8eDIgVNyXq1k0kwy1polmHRC5+bEnp\nTqsIkITHdz73XNjOWTadWm4nsrd5Tb48ow9ZTfYcSehgNsEPsMbt+OcNIW9GGsYX\nupMJuT52vKDJaegeX54cWwQgk2Zn5Pf0sBaYfk3Azl4QQ1QyI9Ei8K2wFtM20QNV\neCST1Ddn8YB6KHb2IFB1wVjmdc+LcI5uu9E3exlh4goF4wqdhMq/MuqXPGQXsqbt\nisiGdMdjWOPapYBdlcZfb+WuveIKfFIIQWwK4we8AnnejHYCpg9fk+z5vtXZra5p\ngGiQrV40DwF0eusRWJEP7yqzTo4iVuWbtg4qEzsEVvyibAn1z+fGFeYuRPYNbf9Q\nhcsD3sB4xJPBu0IMMJH6pyOGw/55D0ctqyXL6bvXbUKYqDiL+jCMEwNpoOqqF0c4\nNsfXZiyixDEfpC/t2THm\n=hKH4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-24T14:42:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKGJjYjMyNTg5MWVjMGViYjMxNDE4YTRlYjNhN2E5MDQ2YzFmNDZiZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6","sha":"8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6"}],"sha":"bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/bcb325891ec0ebb31418a4eb3a7a9046c1f46bd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T15:23:44Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T15:23:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Claude/project remaining work m5h0ek (#45)\n\n* Added Support of Cosmos vector-search capability\n\n* fix: Coderabbit suggestion\n\n* feat: train a real matrix-factorization model for co-purchase recommendations\n\nRecommendationService''s \"customers who bought X also bought Y\" was pure raw\nco-occurrence counting with no training step. Add a genuine trained tier: a\none-class matrix-factorization model (ML.NET) over captured order baskets\n(OrderId x ProductId), with per-product latent vectors ranked by cosine\nsimilarity into a new ProductSimilarityModel container.\n\n- New OrderBaskets container captures raw per-order basket data as durable\n  training input (RecommendationService.RecordOrderAsync), independent of the\n  existing pairwise-count writes.\n- CoPurchaseModelTrainer trains the model as a pure function over domain\n  types; RecommendationModelTrainingWorker retrains it periodically, gated by\n  its own Recommendations:ModelTrainingEnabled flag.\n- GetRecommendationsAsync prefers the trained model per-product, falling back\n  to the original raw-count logic for any product without model coverage yet\n  (new products, thin data, training disabled) — existing behavior and tests\n  are unchanged when no model record exists.\n- Provision the two new Cosmos containers (bicep), bump RecommendationService''s\n  Helm resources for ML.NET''s runtime footprint, and add the new CI secret.\n- Add scripts/ReplaySeedOrders, a one-off tool to backfill training data from\n  the 75 existing seed orders (which predate basket capture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix:CodeRabbitSuggestions\n\n* fix: coderabbit -  backfill baskets directly via Cosmos, dropping the Service Bus replay path entirely.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1dbc9d154280f2901a2583a1ee7dfe01b4d8604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/d1dbc9d154280f2901a2583a1ee7dfe01b4d8604"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/8aa78faf8d9b5dfd4535460998ade9806d6751b6","verification":{"payload":"tree d1dbc9d154280f2901a2583a1ee7dfe01b4d8604\nparent eb9bde36365367ea94fa0f06c5b0b85149f59a9f\nauthor ankitgoelmalviyans <157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com> 1784820224 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784820224 +0530\n\nClaude/project remaining work m5h0ek (#45)\n\n* Added Support of Cosmos vector-search capability\n\n* fix: Coderabbit suggestion\n\n* feat: train a real matrix-factorization model for co-purchase recommendations\n\nRecommendationService''s \"customers who bought X also bought Y\" was pure raw\nco-occurrence counting with no training step. Add a genuine trained tier: a\none-class matrix-factorization model (ML.NET) over captured order baskets\n(OrderId x ProductId), with per-product latent vectors ranked by cosine\nsimilarity into a new ProductSimilarityModel container.\n\n- New OrderBaskets container captures raw per-order basket data as durable\n  training input (RecommendationService.RecordOrderAsync), independent of the\n  existing pairwise-count writes.\n- CoPurchaseModelTrainer trains the model as a pure function over domain\n  types; RecommendationModelTrainingWorker retrains it periodically, gated by\n  its own Recommendations:ModelTrainingEnabled flag.\n- GetRecommendationsAsync prefers the trained model per-product, falling back\n  to the original raw-count logic for any product without model coverage yet\n  (new products, thin data, training disabled) — existing behavior and tests\n  are unchanged when no model record exists.\n- Provision the two new Cosmos containers (bicep), bump RecommendationService''s\n  Helm resources for ML.NET''s runtime footprint, and add the new CI secret.\n- Add scripts/ReplaySeedOrders, a one-off tool to backfill training data from\n  the 75 existing seed orders (which predate basket capture).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix:CodeRabbitSuggestions\n\n* fix: coderabbit -  backfill baskets directly via Cosmos, dropping the Service Bus replay path entirely.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYjIACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA29AQAJaJZiNYkG2lTkiuu1OXPSK+\nV1hLOJrse7vTCIOe9O3LEJ+dInK+tH6/46Z43X9IduyvR5lrrAwyiAgY2tCCSLsB\nx0+GbYT+RblJzpxa8NOAj22YPKl3HsYSpW6FXUVVwXA8MdXwuZy18hMIWJT/kp7q\n2BIcWOQqoCRorgrbG7Bvvk/PTkpVMFPQPfnq3lahodaZy5iAH/l6H8J+yOsOFFc5\nP2T4CZGxH1CdabGEXLlq35z6TPY/OVupQUq3omjgnIqm+s1txW7UtppHotnut2OD\nh63sGGj2KAeRIznfwfZ1mloeKHwkN8zLd8CEgpP4O3GFstqJV2+ebl2oJL+tL1tQ\nWshf5qmeZnZqlfnkM5OeofEAd4L2eSdiPxsDMz0/wSfIqvnfqcE5I5cZIS+K4Eyh\nsaKMiGI2lu9r97+ifQZvHCpFk1ZJlkGCcAev1MCLXbH0E/n1SLG5xvdnzP8TInAh\nATESIS8Mh5KzXKo6bMPct9faC1kt/hrlmCsX9dqHNQZVABxiLk7k/5vj0oJkvNsa\naWpnYr77yps+492P/DjUZAApUooXppDHMO+/rhL6E96GgwLJLLnAL0Ekcdc0MkhF\n6ey6D3wqtfzC+AOnWUB7LoYtvavVcH4Rbipk0nGFymOzyO/B0hVw/5yWps2UCc+t\njl2lzBwp+qe2B0Vs3vOp\n=Xa2L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-23T15:23:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_u