":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/0e8fe723805483dd2706e0ecc643c83f882d939e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:19:10Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T08:19:10Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"feat(ui): wire recommendations and AI search into product-ui\n\nNeither RecommendationService nor AiService''s read endpoints were\ncalled from anywhere in the Angular app — the backend existed, nothing\nin the UI used it. Closes that gap:\n\n- RecommendationService (Angular) + a \"Customers who bought this also\n  bought\" expandable panel on each product row, joining\n  GetRecommendationsAsync''s {productId, count} results against the\n  already-loaded product list client-side (RecommendationService\n  itself has no product-data cache, by design).\n- AiSearchService (Angular) + a new /ai-search page: a plain-language\n  search box that calls AiService''s RAG endpoint and renders the\n  generated answer alongside the books it cites (already denormalised\n  in BookMatch, no join needed there).\n- Two new environment tokens (recommendationApiUrl, aiApiUrl), same\n  #{...}# replacement pattern as the existing five, wired into\n  cd-ui.yml. Unlike Order/Payment, no hard-fail guard if the two\n  secrets are unset — these are supplementary, gracefully-degrading\n  panels, not something the rest of the app depends on.\n\nVerified with a full `ng build --configuration production` — compiles\nclean, new ai-search chunk lazy-loads as expected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35471be65540685dd4c9de0a785c22170002fc11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/35471be65540685dd4c9de0a785c22170