}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/05d6f6e44bcb34234db1ae9fed7e703fd7e6e56c","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKDA1ZDZmNmU0NGJjYjM0MjM0ZGIxYWU5ZmVkN2U3MDNmZDdlNmU1NmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/db781321d3467395fd81d57a939b43eef64cb63e","sha":"db781321d3467395fd81d57a939b43eef64cb63e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/db781321d3467395fd81d57a939b43eef64cb63e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637","sha":"dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637"}],"sha":"05d6f6e44bcb34234db1ae9fed7e703fd7e6e56c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/05d6f6e44bcb34234db1ae9fed7e703fd7e6e56c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T14:34:12Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T14:34:12Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"fix(payment): close Confirm/Cancel race and return proper decline status\n\n- Confirm''s Pending->Captured/Failed transition is now an atomic conditional\n  update (IPaymentRepository.TryClaimAndConfirmAsync, WHERE Status=Pending)\n  instead of a plain tracked-entity save. Closes a real race where two\n  concurrent Confirm calls (a double-click, or a retry) could both pass the\n  Pending check and both commit an outcome + outbox event for one charge.\n- PaymentService now subscribes to order-events (new payment-order-subscription\n  on the existing order-events topic, added to main.bicep) and resolves a\n  Pending payment as Failed when its order is cancelled\n  (HandleOrderCancelledAsync / MarkCancelledIfPendingAsync). Previously\n  PaymentService had no visibility into cancellation at all, so a Confirm\n  racing with a Cancel could charge a card for an order that was just\n  cancelled. The same atomic claim used for Confirm makes this mutually\n  exclusive with a concurrent charge, at the cost of a documented residual\n  limitation: a charge already sent to the gateway when the claim is lost\n  isn''t retroactively refunded (that needs the Stripe webhook path, tracked\n  as PLANNED in docs/ROADMAP.md, not built here).\n- Fixed the actual bug this was covering for: Declined now returns 400 (was\n  200, identical to Charged) so the Angular payment form''s HTTP-status-based\n  success check can no longer treat a declined card as a successful payment.\n  Added AlreadyResolved (409) for the new claim-lost outcome.\n- Typed PaymentService.confirm()''s Angular response instead of Observable<any>.\n- Added a regression test confirming a late InventoryReserved arriving after\n  the customer already cancelled is a safe no-op on the OrderService side\n  (verified InventoryService''s existing reservation-tombstone pattern already\n  handles both orderings of OrderCreated/OrderCancelled correctly — no\n  InventoryService change was needed, just test coverage for OrderService''s\n  half of the contract).\n\nNo EF migration needed for either OrderDb or PaymentDb. All 30 unit tests\n(20 OrderService + 10 PaymentService) pass; Angular production build succeeds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab618403ad2c9fd9d91ed420849c689273c25e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/ab618403ad2c9fd9d91ed420849c689273c25e0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKGRkMjNmNTU2MDcxM2YwN2U3NzUxM2YzZmJkNGUxNDU4NjJkODU2Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/675a4707356b4082cec6230118b824a8d5a4b54a","sha":"675a4707356b4082cec6230118b824a8d5a4b54a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/675a4707356b4082cec6230118b824a8d5a4b54a"}],"sha":"dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/dd23f5560713f07e77513f3fbd4e145862d85637"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/675a4707356b4082cec6230118b824a8d5a4b54a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T13:50:45Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T13:50:45Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"feat(payment): gate checkout behind a real Stripe test-mode pay/cancel step\n\nThe saga previously auto-charged the instant inventory was reserved, with no\nuser interaction and a hardcoded payment method (pm_card_visa) — there was no\nway to actually pay with a card, and no way to cancel before a charge went\nthrough. This replaces that with an explicit customer-facing step:\n\n- New Order status AwaitingPayment, between Pending and Confirmed/Cancelled.\n  OrderOutcomeHandler now reacts to InventoryReserved (previously ignored on\n  the Order side) to move the order there instead of PaymentService charging\n  automatically. The monotonic-transition guard now allows Pending OR\n  AwaitingPayment as source states, since Confirmed/Cancelled now arrive from\n  AwaitingPayment instead of directly from Pending.\n- PaymentService''s InventoryReserved subscriber now only records a Pending\n  Payment row (RecordPendingAsync) — no charge. The actual charge only\n  happens via the new POST /api/payment/{orderId}/confirm, driven by the\n  customer''s explicit Pay action and a real Stripe PaymentMethod id from\n  Stripe Elements (client-side; no raw card data ever reaches this API).\n  Idempotency key is now the Payment row''s own id, since there''s no longer a\n  single inbound event to key off for the charge itself.\n- New POST /api/order/{id}/cancel — a genuine customer command (not a saga\n  event), valid while Pending or AwaitingPayment. Reuses the exact same\n  OrderCancelled → InventoryService release path a payment failure already\n  used, so no InventoryService changes were needed.\n- Angular: a Stripe Elements card form (test-mode publishable key) replaces\n  the old passive \"processing automatically\" message when an order reaches\n  AwaitingPayment, with real Pay/Cancel buttons wired to the endpoints above.\n- Removed the now-dead auto-charge path (old HandleAsync/SaveChargeAsync/\n  TransientPaymentException, the hardcoded Payments:DefaultPaymentMethod\n  config) rather than leaving it alongside the new one.\n\nNo new EF migrations needed for either OrderDb or PaymentDb — only enum\nvalues and application-code behavior changed, not entity shape. Unit tests\nupdated/added for both OrderOutcomeHandler (AwaitingPayment transitions,\nCancelByCustomerAsync) and ProcessReservationHandler (RecordPendingAsync/\nConfirmAsync in place of the old single-shot HandleAsync); all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"025258c6a11fff7073c69bbc8bd74bbfb97ca93a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/025258c6a11fff7073c69bbc8bd74bbfb97ca93a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/675a4707356b4082cec6230118b824a8d5a4b54a","verification":{"