6Ov0NyM8rZsPU\n=nouD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T17:10:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/f0a84c2af28e7d993e179fe7a381ff38f38c637e","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKGYwYTg0YzJhZjI4ZTdkOTkzZTE3OWZlN2EzODFmZjM4ZjM4YzYzN2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/8a46db90a4d3b49777b712835dd9ea1cf43f585a","sha":"8a46db90a4d3b49777b712835dd9ea1cf43f585a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/8a46db90a4d3b49777b712835dd9ea1cf43f585a"}],"sha":"f0a84c2af28e7d993e179fe7a381ff38f38c637e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/f0a84c2af28e7d993e179fe7a381ff38f38c637e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/8a46db90a4d3b49777b712835dd9ea1cf43f585a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T11:42:47Z","email":"157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T11:42:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Update documents (#21)\n\n* fix(security): clear all .NET dependency vulns + safe npm subset\n\n.NET (all 3 services now report 0 vulnerable NuGet packages):\n- Bump OpenTelemetry.* 1.9.0 -> 1.16.0 (fixes GHSA-4625-4j76-fww9 OTLP disk-retry\n  blob injection, and GHSA-g94r-2vxg-569j in OpenTelemetry.Api).\n- Add explicit Microsoft.Bcl.Memory 9.0.14 override — OTLP 1.16.0 pulls the\n  vulnerable 9.0.0 transitively (GHSA-73j8-2gch-69rq, Base64Url OOB-read DoS,\n  High); 9.0.14 is the first patched release.\n- Remove AutoMapper.Extensions.Microsoft.DependencyInjection 12.0.1 entirely\n  (High, GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x). It was registered but never used — no Profiles,\n  no IMapper injection, no Map<> calls — so removing the dead dependency\n  eliminates the advisory rather than chasing AutoMapper''s post-v13 commercial\n  licensing. Dropped from the API project and the orphaned StartupExtensions\n  project, plus both AddAutoMapper() calls.\n- Add explicit System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt 8.8.0 to Product + Inventory to\n  override the vulnerable 7.0.3 that JwtBearer 8.0.0 pulls transitively\n  (GHSA-59j7-ghrg-fj52, JWT DoS). 8.8.0 matches AuthService, proven compatible.\n\nnpm (safe, non-breaking subset only — verified the Angular prod build still\npasses): non-force `npm audit fix` took the product-ui tree from 71 -> 50\nadvisories, removing the lone critical (shell-quote) and ~20 others. Only\npackage-lock.json changed (no direct-dependency bumps).\n\nThe remaining ~50 npm advisories are gated behind an Angular 17 (EOL) major\nupgrade and can''t be fixed in place — documented as a staged migration in\ndocs/ROADMAP.md. Most are build-time devDependencies (never shipped to the\nbrowser); the browser-shipped @angular/* runtime advisories need the migration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: reframe devDependency advisories as build-env supply-chain risk\n\nAddress CodeRabbit review on the Dependabot-vulnerabilities PR: the previous\nwording called build-time devDependency advisories \"low real-world exposure\",\nwhich understates them. They''re a distinct risk — build-environment supply-chain\n(arbitrary code via install/lifecycle scripts on CI runners and dev machines),\nnot reduced risk — as opposed to the browser-shipped @angular/* runtime\npackages. Now framed as two categories that both matter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: consolidate all docs under docs/, delete stale/redundant files\n\nDocumentation audit + cleanup. docs/ is now the single home for all\nplatform/architecture docs; root README links to it and component/operational\nREADMEs stay next to their code (infrastructure/istio/, azure-pipelines-reference/).\n\nDeleted (9) — factually wrong about the current architecture, or generic\nmaterial superseded by the docs/ set:\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/README_SCA.md (Kafka \"integration-ready\", Azure App\n  Services, product \"quantity\" — none current)\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/BookStore.ProductService/docs/ReadMe.md (2-line stub)\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/product-ui/README_Angular_Product_UI.md (azurewebsites.net\n  URLs, /api/login, getInventory() — all wrong now)\n- misc docs/* (6): Misc, git-workflow-guide, yaml-overview (all Azure DevOps /\n  Kafka / DuckDNS / .NET 7 era), containerization (generic, superseded by\n  docs/KUBERNETES.md), Copilot training (unrelated), InverviewQuestions\n  (generic C# checklist, overlaps docs/INTERVIEW_QA.md)\n\nUpdated (5) — fixed drift from recent changes (Quantity removal, /decrement\nendpoint, Outbox/Inbox, Istio, IMessagePublisher):\n- README.md — repo-structure diagram now shows docs/ + infrastructure/istio/,\n  drops deleted misc docs/, adds a docs/ pointer\n- docs/PRD.md — Product has no quantity; added /decrement; inventory inits at 0\n- docs/TRD.md — IMessagePublisher signature (correlationId/traceParent); new\n  ADR-15 (minimal Istio mesh)\n- docs/DOTNET_CONCEPTS.md — IMessagePublisher is Singleton not Scoped; added\n  Outbox to the DI list and the /decrement route\n- docs/HLD.md — corrected the stale \"set quantity from the event\" line to\n  zero-init + explicit restock/decrement\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review on UpdateDocuments PR (Helm tree formatting)\n\nauthservice/productservice/inventoryservice were combined onto a single tree\nline in README.md''s repository-structure diagram, breaking the tree format.\nSplit into three separate entries, one per chart directory (matches the\nactual infrastructure/helm/ layout).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1625c24582607f652f523ec8f2ba1627f758d54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/d1625c24582607f652f523ec8f2ba1627f758d54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/8a46db90a4d3b49777b712835dd9ea1cf43f585a","verification":{"payload":"tree d1625c24582607f652f523ec8f2ba1627f758d54\nparent 32ac21339c3e03973ecf71a3cef9396c124d3fb7\nauthor ankitgoelmalviyans <157928570+ankitgoelmalviyans@users.noreply.github.com> 1783510967 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783510967 +0530\n\nUpdate documents (#21)\n\n* fix(security): clear all .NET dependency vulns + safe npm subset\n\n.NET (all 3 services now report 0 vulnerable NuGet packages):\n- Bump OpenTelemetry.* 1.9.0 -> 1.16.0 (fixes GHSA-4625-4j76-fww9 OTLP disk-retry\n  blob injection, and GHSA-g94r-2vxg-569j in OpenTelemetry.Api).\n- Add explicit Microsoft.Bcl.Memory 9.0.14 override — OTLP 1.16.0 pulls the\n  vulnerable 9.0.0 transitively (GHSA-73j8-2gch-69rq, Base64Url OOB-read DoS,\n  High); 9.0.14 is the first patched release.\n- Remove AutoMapper.Extensions.Microsoft.DependencyInjection 12.0.1 entirely\n  (High, GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x). It was registered but never used — no Profiles,\n  no IMapper injection, no Map<> calls — so removing the dead dependency\n  eliminates the advisory rather than chasing AutoMapper''s post-v13 commercial\n  licensing. Dropped from the API project and the orphaned StartupExtensions\n  project, plus both AddAutoMapper() calls.\n- Add explicit System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt 8.8.0 to Product + Inventory to\n  override the vulnerable 7.0.3 that JwtBearer 8.0.0 pulls transitively\n  (GHSA-59j7-ghrg-fj52, JWT DoS). 8.8.0 matches AuthService, proven compatible.\n\nnpm (safe, non-breaking subset only — verified the Angular prod build still\npasses): non-force `npm audit fix` took the product-ui tree from 71 -> 50\nadvisories, removing the lone critical (shell-quote) and ~20 others. Only\npackage-lock.json changed (no direct-dependency bumps).\n\nThe remaining ~50 npm advisories are gated behind an Angular 17 (EOL) major\nupgrade and can''t be fixed in place — documented as a staged migration in\ndocs/ROADMAP.md. Most are build-time devDependencies (never shipped to the\nbrowser); the browser-shipped @angular/* runtime advisories need the migration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: reframe devDependency advisories as build-env supply-chain risk\n\nAddress CodeRabbit review on the Dependabot-vulnerabilities PR: the previous\nwording called build-time devDependency advisories \"low real-world exposure\",\nwhich understates them. They''re a distinct risk — build-environment supply-chain\n(arbitrary code via install/lifecycle scripts on CI runners and dev machines),\nnot reduced risk — as opposed to the browser-shipped @angular/* runtime\npackages. Now framed as two categories that both matter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: consolidate all docs under docs/, delete stale/redundant files\n\nDocumentation audit + cleanup. docs/ is now the single home for all\nplatform/architecture docs; root README links to it and component/operational\nREADMEs stay next to their code (infrastructure/istio/, azure-pipelines-reference/).\n\nDeleted (9) — factually wrong about the current architecture, or generic\nmaterial superseded by the docs/ set:\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/README_SCA.md (Kafka \"integration-ready\", Azure App\n  Services, product \"quantity\" — none current)\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/BookStore.ProductService/docs/ReadMe.md (2-line stub)\n- BookStore.ProductSCA/product-ui/README_Angular_Product_UI.md (azurewebsites.net\n  URLs, /api/login, getInventory() — all wrong now)\n- misc docs/* (6): Misc, git-workflow-guide, yaml-overview (all Azure DevOps /\n  Kafka / DuckDNS / .NET 7 era), containerization (generic, superseded by\n  docs/KUBERNETES.md), Copilot training (unrelated), InverviewQuestions\n  (generic C# checklist, overlaps docs/INTERVIEW_QA.md)\n\nUpdated (5) — fixed drift from recent changes (Quantity removal, /decrement\nendpoint, Outbox/Inbox, Istio, IMessagePublisher):\n- README.md — repo-structure diagram now shows docs/ + infrastructure/istio/,\n  drops deleted misc docs/, adds a docs/ pointer\n- docs/PRD.md — Product has no quantity; added /decrement; inventory inits at 0\n- docs/TRD.md — IMessagePublisher signature (correlationId/traceParent); new\n  ADR-15 (minimal Istio mesh)\n- docs/DOTNET_CONCEPTS.md — IMessagePublisher is Singleton not Scoped; added\n  Outbox to the DI list and the /decrement route\n- docs/HLD.md — corrected the stale \"set quantity from the event\" line to\n  zero-init + explicit restock/decrement\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review on UpdateDocuments PR (Helm tree formatting)\n\nauthservice/productservice/inventoryservice were combined onto a single tree\nline in README.md''s repository-structure diagram, breaking the tree format.\nSplit into three separate entries, one per chart directory (matches the\nactual infrastructure/helm/ layout).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTje3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAawQAEcEadkxhTRoug+e5DyQS21H\nmDkxnOJkuzd/CtNc8oiIxeZjaE2lkOWAb1Tf+D/7S1U8RBUh+P5qh3nKec7KCu8j\nAv7n/FOQdXiVI8whJrxdfW+i9il+soO+0PNDsECaH2IXABf1Qxyr4+FWVBHgcb+E\n7/wQuRk0a+rSApPF6XpfHebEAp2ZgzfSVYbpjI+PK8kVq8ijtVQ0u1ZEZR/aPonO\nadEXjHMLQ6ZCIKKjGu3nuLYOWw2rzJ3wXexIYsiTPHkAixvK8tagq0xEEZjpA3jA\n4FYsIVNOzac1C+HEhtmd1l+ocMhOkig+Zxfj0b/REAoTllI+HqJXrgiP+4Rk9I4m\nnt0ReRCee0j+6b5F/wTEPEeWxYbCbfiSNixj+2YUm5J6NW3qe3LxnkNYf7eFCNq9\nI9qHWtyMj1fevwt1VSA5L61I2bbJkaaYtX4kvLApiyUaKnEscQVVHFMSIhcf/ahM\nxYOxdhEdd6AkUN67+u6yVVK1+UuX+9COpRpvTnrjeVLExIZIz6HyEMf4ijmSIzZf\n5JlLS5OY9pbfEHNjD/4T7449hurFvh0spRZCEU/R2TnV1Fi1EX/EGJVt6qug9UbH\n2xMQrUK/F7Qc9aTZYoptf7nGkhiqCPfuGaCGQ67+rkJ823FUEqu4X9EPIgWwXtfr\nM81boCREi+zp9Y+kBnEI\n=14oI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE----