kStore/commit/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419","sha":"167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419"}],"sha":"0fbeff8f03dc5c4e91fd99030a99e22589ff0925","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/0fbeff8f03dc5c4e91fd99030a99e22589ff0925"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:54:07Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:54:07Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"fix: address CodeRabbit review on PR #19 (Istio mesh)\n\n- Pin ISTIO_VERSION=1.30.2 in infra-bicep.yml instead of curl|sh always\n  pulling latest — a rerun months from now could otherwise silently install\n  a different, untested istioctl/control-plane version.\n- Create the bookstore namespace (idempotent) before applying\n  peer-authentication.yaml in infra-bicep.yml. That workflow never otherwise\n  creates it (only cd-costopt.yml does) — on a genuinely fresh cluster, the\n  exact scenario this \"Always-On\" infra workflow exists for, the apply would\n  fail outright.\n- Split virtual-service-resilience.yaml''s retry policy by method: 5xx retries\n  now only apply to idempotent GET requests. Retrying a 5xx on a write means\n  the request already reached the server — we can''t tell if it applied before\n  failing, so retrying risked Envoy resending an already-successful write\n  (e.g. double-decrementing stock via the future decrement endpoint). Writes\n  keep only connection-level retry conditions (reset/connect-failure/\n  refused-stream), never 5xx.\n- Nil-safe guard in bookstore-lib''s _deployment.yaml:\n  {{ .Values.istio.inject }} -> {{ (.Values.istio | default dict).inject }}.\n  All 3 current chart consumers set istio.inject explicitly, but a future\n  4th service chart that omits the key entirely would otherwise hit a\n  nil-pointer template render failure instead of safely defaulting to \"not\n  meshed\". Verified with `helm template --set istio=null`.\n- docs/LLD.md: reworded the OTLP backend recommendation — it claimed\n  Application Insights was the \"only\" $0-pod option while the table two\n  lines above it already listed Splunk Observability Cloud as also $0-pods.\n  Now framed as \"recommended default\" among multiple managed options.\n- infrastructure/istio/README.md: fixed a markdown table missing its 3rd\n  column on the last two rows, and a `kubectl get pods -n bookstore\n  -n istio-system` troubleshooting command that only honored the last -n\n  flag and silently never checked bookstore pods at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"080649367fc88a9b256e186b56a02ce83441b157","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/080649367fc88a9b256e186b56a02ce83441b157"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419","node_id":"C_kwDOOcYFSNoAKDE2N2E1Yjk2Yzg2ZWRiZjc5NTcwMjcxNzBmYjU1ZDhkMWM5ZTA0MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commit/c4e1b341d4818bad056084165a04e40106a18e3f","sha":"c4e1b341d4818bad056084165a04e40106a18e3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/c4e1b341d4818bad056084165a04e40106a18e3f"}],"sha":"167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/167a5b96c86edbf7957027170fb55d8d1c9e0419"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ankitgoelmalviyans","id":157928570,"login":"ankitgoelmalviyans","node_id":"U_kgDOCWnMeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/c4e1b341d4818bad056084165a04e40106a18e3f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:26:08Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:26:08Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"feat: minimal Istio mesh for Product + Inventory (mTLS, retries, no gateway)\n\nScoped deliberately small for the single Standard_B2s node:\n- istiod control plane only, no Istio ingress gateway (NGINX stays the front\n  door), tuned-down resource requests (infrastructure/istio/istio-operator-minimal.yaml)\n- Sidecar injection opt-in per-pod, scoped to Product + Inventory only via\n  sidecar.istio.io/inject in bookstore-lib''s deployment template. AuthService\n  is deliberately not meshed.\n- mTLS is PERMISSIVE, not STRICT: NGINX Ingress isn''t meshed and routes all\n  real user traffic to these two services — STRICT would reject that traffic\n  outright and take down the live site. See peer-authentication.yaml.\n- VirtualService/DestinationRule gives InventoryService retries + timeout +\n  connection-pool limits by default (safe — NGINX bypasses Istio''s L7 routing\n  entirely, so this only affects meshed-to-meshed calls, none of which exist\n  yet — this is groundwork for a future OrderService).\n- AuthorizationPolicy kept as a reference file, NOT applied: no real\n  synchronous caller exists between these services today, and a naive\n  restrictive policy risks blocking the pod''s own health probe.\n- Fault-injection demo file for actually proving the retry policy works,\n  not applied by default.\n- Istio install wired into infra-bicep.yml''s existing workflow_dispatch\n  pipeline (alongside NGINX/cert-manager install), not a manual local step.\n- Fluent Bit''s container allowlist now includes istio-proxy, so Envoy''s own\n  access logs reach Splunk instead of being silently dropped by the same\n  filter that excludes fluent-bit''s own logs.\n- docs/ROADMAP.md, HLD.md, LLD.md updated to reflect what''s actually\n  implemented vs still planned (weighted canary needs real v1/v2 subsets,\n  which don''t exist yet).\n- docs/LLD.md: new \"Where to send it\" section comparing OTLP backend options\n  (Azure Application Insights, Splunk Observability Cloud, Jaeger, Tempo) for\n  Otel:OtlpEndpoint, since Splunk Cloud Platform (the log product already in\n  use) has no native OTLP receiver.\n\ninfrastructure/istio/README.md has the full install/verify/rollback sequence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7913553018ba7b9fa1e59d39e324ab304984e1cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/7913553018ba7b9fa1e59d39e324ab304984e1cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/co