,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/commits/64ca979091d1b9fdcf55db6a29c3657eef430747/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T12:25:37Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T12:25:37Z","email":"ankitmalviyans@gmail.com","name":"ankitgoelmalviyans"},"message":"Merge_Log Off — removed entirely, along with Merge_Log_Key. We don''t need the kubernetes filter''s own JSON-merging behavior anymore since we''re doing extraction ourselves, and it''s one less thing that could still be silently eating fields.\nRewrote flatten.lua to use plain Lua string.match patterns instead of cjson.decode — no external library dependency at all, since this image''s Fluent Bit build doesn''t ship cjson. It pulls Level, MessageTemplate, Application, CorrelationId, TraceId, SpanOperationName directly via pattern match; if a line isn''t valid Serilog JSON (e.g. a Console.WriteLine), nothing matches, changed stays false, and the record passes through completely untouched — same non-destructive guarantee as before, just without the crash.","tree":{"sha":"d5a45ad7e72e99925c9b98d56b12853a28cab941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/trees/d5a45ad7e72e99925c9b98d56b12853a28cab941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ankitgoelmalviyans/BookStore/git/commits/64ca979091d1b9fdcf55db6a29c3657eef430747","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/157928570?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ankitgoelmalviyans/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"http