{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/9fd9cbb9a9e64c774133e61f159558c880719b75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:40:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:40:05Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Sync the README with the site and fix two stale figures\n\nAuditing the README against the page turned up three real mismatches,\ntwo of them wrong on the site as well.\n\nDomain count: the page carries ten domain cards since the procurement\nplatform was added, but both counters still said nine. Corrected in the\nhero stat, the tile and the README table.\n\nPublic sector stack: the 2026 CV restates that project as ASP.NET Web\nAPI, Entity Framework, SQL Server, Azure and Serilog — Svelte and\nMongoDB are no longer part of it. The page and the README both still\nlisted the old pair. (The depth chart was already computed from the new\nlist, so its figures were right.) AI & PropTech gains GCP for the same\nreason.\n\nREADME otherwise brought level with the skills section: gRPC, Auth0 /\nOIDC, Kong Gateway, Next.js, Bicep, Serilog and Application Insights\nadded to the badge groups; Desktop and Testing split apart so Electron,\nMoq, Playwright, k6 and Codacy each have a home; an AI-assisted\ndevelopment group for Copilot, Cursor and Claude; and English (B2) in\nthe header record.\n\n\"How I work\" rewritten from the new CV — hexagonal architecture and DDD,\nOAuth2/OIDC at service boundaries, observability wired in from the start\nagainst SLA/RTO/RPO targets, k6 and Playwright, four isolated\nenvironments, architect on a team of ten.\n\nRepository notes updated: seven inline-SVG diagrams, not one, and the\nno-JS behaviour of the architecture tabs described.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled:\ncounters 8/16/10/4, tiles 113/16/12/10, ten domain cards, seven tabs,\nnine skill cards, no stale chips, no overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"7e3ac42a98759c91af53bd8dec3946e993df86f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/7e3ac42a98759c91af53bd8dec3946e993df86f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/9fd9cbb9a9e64c774133e61f159558c880719b75","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e3ac42a98759c91af53bd8dec3946e993df86f5\nparent 7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929605 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929605 +0000\n\nSync the README with the site and fix two stale figures\n\nAuditing the README against the page turned up three real mismatches,\ntwo of them wrong on the site as well.\n\nDomain count: the page carries ten domain cards since the procurement\nplatform was added, but both counters still said nine. Corrected in the\nhero stat, the tile and the README table.\n\nPublic sector stack: the 2026 CV restates that project as ASP.NET Web\nAPI, Entity Framework, SQL Server, Azure and Serilog — Svelte and\nMongoDB are no longer part of it. The page and the README both still\nlisted the old pair. (The depth chart was already computed from the new\nlist, so its figures were right.) AI & PropTech gains GCP for the same\nreason.\n\nREADME otherwise brought level with the skills section: gRPC, Auth0 /\nOIDC, Kong Gateway, Next.js, Bicep, Serilog and Application Insights\nadded to the badge groups; Desktop and Testing split apart so Electron,\nMoq, Playwright, k6 and Codacy each have a home; an AI-assisted\ndevelopment group for Copilot, Cursor and Claude; and English (B2) in\nthe header record.\n\n\"How I work\" rewritten from the new CV — hexagonal architecture and DDD,\nOAuth2/OIDC at service boundaries, observability wired in from the start\nagainst SLA/RTO/RPO targets, k6 and Playwright, four isolated\nenvironments, architect on a team of ten.\n\nRepository notes updated: seven inline-SVG diagrams, not one, and the\nno-JS behaviour of the architecture tabs described.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled:\ncounters 8/16/10/4, tiles 113/16/12/10, ten domain cards, seven tabs,\nnine skill cards, no stale chips, no overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEkaESNc\ntJzFN1db2IdGA3RN98IhFwLBThOaAr2Evo1ezmbvpvQ5sHE4IzuWIsrLuXhvIjfXTUhLr3Bjy/nc\nJws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:40:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/9fd9cbb9a9e64c774133e61f159558c880719b75","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKDlmZDljYmI5YTllNjRjNzc0MTMzZTYxZjE1OTU1OGM4ODA3MTliNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462","sha":"7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462"}],"sha":"9fd9cbb9a9e64c774133e61f159558c880719b75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/9fd9cbb9a9e64c774133e61f159558c880719b75"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:35:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:35:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add the in-development stack to the skills section\n\nCurrent builds that are not in the CV and are not named, since they are\nstill in development: a cross-platform Electron desktop app with signed\nauto-updates over a shared React core, Supabase for data and auth,\nTipTap for rich text, Playwright on the critical flows, containerised\nbehind nginx.\n\nFolded the earlier \"Side projects\" card into this one — a single\n\"Building now\" card covering both the in-development products and the\nself-directed repos, marked as outside the CV so it is not read as\nprofessional history. Same in the README badge block.\n\nStack read from the anycourse monorepo''s own manifests. The other\ncurrent repository could not be read: add_repo refuses it because it\nsits under a different owner than this session''s sources, so its\ntechnologies are not represented here yet.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: nine skill cards, no horizontal overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"dde61566a90baf91cfb656ae59972f44a4317f7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/dde61566a90baf91cfb656ae59972f44a4317f7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462","verification":{"payload":"tree dde61566a90baf91cfb656ae59972f44a4317f7a\nparent 326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929310 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929310 +0000\n\nAdd the in-development stack to the skills section\n\nCurrent builds that are not in the CV and are not named, since they are\nstill in development: a cross-platform Electron desktop app with signed\nauto-updates over a shared React core, Supabase for data and auth,\nTipTap for rich text, Playwright on the critical flows, containerised\nbehind nginx.\n\nFolded the earlier \"Side projects\" card into this one — a single\n\"Building now\" card covering both the in-development products and the\nself-directed repos, marked as outside the CV so it is not read as\nprofessional history. Same in the README badge block.\n\nStack read from the anycourse monorepo''s own manifests. The other\ncurrent repository could not be read: add_repo refuses it because it\nsits under a different owner than this session''s sources, so its\ntechnologies are not represented here yet.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: nine skill cards, no horizontal overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCF6Walr\nvZ7bSRfdPm7eiIj5TIU1h/s/tByV7yWk3/3oSPeCg3dN/YjhgAtCqiCVQOEsQye5VF7MYWo2ULUD\nGQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:35:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKDdlNDVmODFiODhjMzVjYzQ3ZTY2MDdhZWE2ZDc2ZDhhOTg0ZTM0NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589","sha":"326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589"}],"sha":"7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/7e45f81b88c35cc47e6607aea6d76d8a984e3462"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:33:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:33:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Rebuild against the 2026 CV, including the current platform\n\nThe CV the site was built from turned out to be last year''s. This is the\n13/06/2026 version, and it changes a lot more than the date.\n\nassets/Phuong-Tran-CV.pdf replaced with the real file, so the download\nfinally serves the current CV rather than the 2025 one.\n\nNew, and the reason the site felt incomplete: the AI-driven enterprise\nquotation and procurement platform, 6/2025 to present, architect\nengineer on a team of ten. It now appears in three places — a Work card\nmarked as ongoing, a full timeline entry, and its own architecture tab,\nwhich leads the set. Terraform provisioning four identical environments\nis the part of it worth drawing, so the caption says why.\n\nFigures recomputed over 16 projects and a 98-month span:\n\n  .NET / C#  97 -> 113     SQL Server  36 -> 49\n  TypeScript 65 ->  68     plus GitHub Actions 34, ASP.NET Web API 29,\n  Angular    49 ->  65     Serilog 29 and Terraform 26 entering the top\n  EF         39 ->  55     ten; Azure 36 -> 52\n\nTitle is Senior Full-stack Developer throughout, and the summary now\nleads with owning systems end to end rather than listing layers.\n\nSkills gained what the new CV adds: gRPC, Auth0/OIDC, Next.js, Bicep,\nSerilog, Application Insights, Playwright, k6, hexagonal architecture,\nDDD, Electron.js, and AI-assisted development with Copilot, Cursor and\nClaude. English is now stated as B2.\n\nWorth noting: the new CV''s GitHub handle is phuongfullstack, so the\nmismatch flagged earlier is resolved — the site was already right.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: seven tabs each showing exactly one panel, all seven\nrendering without JS, counters landing on the new values, no horizontal\noverflow, no page errors, no company names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"049b0fc0443c6cb0c2e1fce2718775e21efe2b48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/049b0fc0443c6cb0c2e1fce2718775e21efe2b48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589","verification":{"payload":"tree 049b0fc0443c6cb0c2e1fce2718775e21efe2b48\nparent b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929184 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789929184 +0000\n\nRebuild against the 2026 CV, including the current platform\n\nThe CV the site was built from turned out to be last year''s. This is the\n13/06/2026 version, and it changes a lot more than the date.\n\nassets/Phuong-Tran-CV.pdf replaced with the real file, so the download\nfinally serves the current CV rather than the 2025 one.\n\nNew, and the reason the site felt incomplete: the AI-driven enterprise\nquotation and procurement platform, 6/2025 to present, architect\nengineer on a team of ten. It now appears in three places — a Work card\nmarked as ongoing, a full timeline entry, and its own architecture tab,\nwhich leads the set. Terraform provisioning four identical environments\nis the part of it worth drawing, so the caption says why.\n\nFigures recomputed over 16 projects and a 98-month span:\n\n  .NET / C#  97 -> 113     SQL Server  36 -> 49\n  TypeScript 65 ->  68     plus GitHub Actions 34, ASP.NET Web API 29,\n  Angular    49 ->  65     Serilog 29 and Terraform 26 entering the top\n  EF         39 ->  55     ten; Azure 36 -> 52\n\nTitle is Senior Full-stack Developer throughout, and the summary now\nleads with owning systems end to end rather than listing layers.\n\nSkills gained what the new CV adds: gRPC, Auth0/OIDC, Next.js, Bicep,\nSerilog, Application Insights, Playwright, k6, hexagonal architecture,\nDDD, Electron.js, and AI-assisted development with Copilot, Cursor and\nClaude. English is now stated as B2.\n\nWorth noting: the new CV''s GitHub handle is phuongfullstack, so the\nmismatch flagged earlier is resolved — the site was already right.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: seven tabs each showing exactly one panel, all seven\nrendering without JS, counters landing on the new values, no horizontal\noverflow, no page errors, no company names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJEtCjyT\n9XM8k0JmFYOV+H5FM8iHXxiS2GP/7h7O88fDUQhSN/16Q7mcqtXOVOYBDNXxxs7bpMZZZEXi/kYt\n3go=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:33:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKDMyNmZhMDNjZWJlZGI5NWYyNGU2ODhhZGIzMTIxNjRmNDZkOTg1ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591","sha":"b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591"}],"sha":"326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/326fa03cebedb95f24e688adb312164f46d98589"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:23:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:23:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Six architecture models, side-project stack, no company names\n\nThree changes in one pass.\n\nHow I build: one generic diagram replaced with six, each a shape the\nwork actually took — microservices behind a gateway, serverless and\nevent-driven, a realtime device link, an embeddable widget with AI\nworkers, an ETL and migration pipeline, and a consumer app across a CMS\nand three billing rails. Each carries one line of reasoning for why it\nis shaped that way, which is the part a diagram alone cannot say.\n\nPresented as tabs rather than a slider: every model is visible as a\nchoice, any one is a single click away, arrow keys move between them,\nand each is deep-linkable. A slider hides five of six behind an\ninteraction and has no good keyboard story. With JavaScript off no\npanel is hidden, so all six render stacked.\n\nSkills: added a card for self-directed work, built from the public\nnon-fork repositories rather than the CV — Next.js, Tailwind, Radix,\nElectron, Bun, a .NET 10 API with SignalR hubs, Supabase, the Gemini\nAPI, Playwright and Vitest, deployed on Vercel, Render and Caddy. Kept\nseparate from the CV-sourced cards so professional and personal work\nare not conflated.\n\nExperience: company names removed in favour of what the setting was —\nproduct delivery partner, enterprise software services, offshore product\nengineering, software outsourcing studio. Same in the README table.\n\nFixed while building: the diagram generator prefixed \"0 0\" onto viewBox\nvalues that already carried it, so every SVG had a malformed viewBox,\nfell back to its intrinsic size and spilled its nodes over the caption.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: each tab shows exactly one panel, all six render without\nJS, no horizontal overflow, no page errors, and no company name is left\nanywhere in the rendered text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"6e99ef473f431bc90653b44ebeda79b7d5fbbe9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/6e99ef473f431bc90653b44ebeda79b7d5fbbe9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e99ef473f431bc90653b44ebeda79b7d5fbbe9e\nparent b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789928627 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789928627 +0000\n\nSix architecture models, side-project stack, no company names\n\nThree changes in one pass.\n\nHow I build: one generic diagram replaced with six, each a shape the\nwork actually took — microservices behind a gateway, serverless and\nevent-driven, a realtime device link, an embeddable widget with AI\nworkers, an ETL and migration pipeline, and a consumer app across a CMS\nand three billing rails. Each carries one line of reasoning for why it\nis shaped that way, which is the part a diagram alone cannot say.\n\nPresented as tabs rather than a slider: every model is visible as a\nchoice, any one is a single click away, arrow keys move between them,\nand each is deep-linkable. A slider hides five of six behind an\ninteraction and has no good keyboard story. With JavaScript off no\npanel is hidden, so all six render stacked.\n\nSkills: added a card for self-directed work, built from the public\nnon-fork repositories rather than the CV — Next.js, Tailwind, Radix,\nElectron, Bun, a .NET 10 API with SignalR hubs, Supabase, the Gemini\nAPI, Playwright and Vitest, deployed on Vercel, Render and Caddy. Kept\nseparate from the CV-sourced cards so professional and personal work\nare not conflated.\n\nExperience: company names removed in favour of what the setting was —\nproduct delivery partner, enterprise software services, offshore product\nengineering, software outsourcing studio. Same in the README table.\n\nFixed while building: the diagram generator prefixed \"0 0\" onto viewBox\nvalues that already carried it, so every SVG had a malformed viewBox,\nfell back to its intrinsic size and spilled its nodes over the caption.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: each tab shows exactly one panel, all six render without\nJS, no horizontal overflow, no page errors, and no company name is left\nanywhere in the rendered text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOYYAyPQ\n56U0K7QXmbXu0XXKzAFQya7sb7Rhjxp4hArGKqX6xPJ9S12revsGFydILQYPMQHCoqnO84RfSBTA\nQAI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:23:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKGIxYjJmNjE3Mjc5YThiZDdkYWE4N2I1MGNhYTgzMjZkNzRiZjk1OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9","sha":"b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9"}],"sha":"b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/b1b2f617279a8bd7daa87b50caa8326d74bf9591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:16:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T18:16:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Detail the skills section and fix the month arithmetic\n\nSkills (section 03, was \"Stack\"): each card now carries the evidence\nbehind the chips rather than only the chips — how many projects used\nit and since when, plus a sentence on what it was actually used for,\ndrawn from the CV''s own project responsibilities. Added the parts of\nthe CV''s skills list the page had dropped: Trello, TaxJar, work\nbreakdown and planning, and English proficiency.\n\nMonth arithmetic: the depth chart counted elapsed months while the Work\ncards counted inclusively, so a project running Mar 2022 to Mar 2023 was\n13 months in one place and 12 in the other. Inclusive is the correct\nreading, so every chart figure was one month short per project:\n\n  .NET / C#  84 -> 97      SQL Server  32 -> 36\n  TypeScript 58 -> 65      Azure       33 -> 36\n  Angular    44 -> 49      JavaScript  20 -> 23\n  EF         35 -> 39      Java / AWS  17 -> 18, Svelte 14 -> 16\n\nThe dated-history span is 83 months, not 82, and two domain spans were\nalso off by one: Education & enterprise web 29 -> 30, Blockchain 10 -> 11.\nBar widths rescaled against the new maximum.\n\nTwo skill-card counts were scoped wrong on first write: Backend is 14\nprojects (the Java API work counts too), and Desktop is 2 WPF projects\nfrom 2021 — WinForms, UWP, Flutter and Android are in the CV''s skills\nlist but not tied to any dated project, so they stay as chips without\nfeeding the count.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: no horizontal overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"3683d6dfbca6bd095ac931937d66915fcf82902a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/3683d6dfbca6bd095ac931937d66915fcf82902a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3683d6dfbca6bd095ac931937d66915fcf82902a\nparent 12eca76392330706653c1f19dfc66e74135e034c\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789928188 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789928188 +0000\n\nDetail the skills section and fix the month arithmetic\n\nSkills (section 03, was \"Stack\"): each card now carries the evidence\nbehind the chips rather than only the chips — how many projects used\nit and since when, plus a sentence on what it was actually used for,\ndrawn from the CV''s own project responsibilities. Added the parts of\nthe CV''s skills list the page had dropped: Trello, TaxJar, work\nbreakdown and planning, and English proficiency.\n\nMonth arithmetic: the depth chart counted elapsed months while the Work\ncards counted inclusively, so a project running Mar 2022 to Mar 2023 was\n13 months in one place and 12 in the other. Inclusive is the correct\nreading, so every chart figure was one month short per project:\n\n  .NET / C#  84 -> 97      SQL Server  32 -> 36\n  TypeScript 58 -> 65      Azure       33 -> 36\n  Angular    44 -> 49      JavaScript  20 -> 23\n  EF         35 -> 39      Java / AWS  17 -> 18, Svelte 14 -> 16\n\nThe dated-history span is 83 months, not 82, and two domain spans were\nalso off by one: Education & enterprise web 29 -> 30, Blockchain 10 -> 11.\nBar widths rescaled against the new maximum.\n\nTwo skill-card counts were scoped wrong on first write: Backend is 14\nprojects (the Java API work counts too), and Desktop is 2 WPF projects\nfrom 2021 — WinForms, UWP, Flutter and Android are in the CV''s skills\nlist but not tied to any dated project, so they stay as chips without\nfeeding the count.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion: no horizontal overflow, no page errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO1N+ToX\nZ6MIt8G0OtNs6nnNci5fCgzQxbr72auM1KNiox9D2Cpzr8njditjrR39Kz+9kayIKCQRbRU7isdX\n6Q0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:16:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/b029fb0e8a9c7b3d21df5392bace9d34552a21b9","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKGIwMjlmYjBlOGE5YzdiM2QyMWRmNTM5MmJhY2