ngfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/a9258ef822c9e7aa25131a08736eee7a42c515c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/de0ed910830ce7288c816d9267f8fa2f3466f6a5","verification":{"payload":"tree a9258ef822c9e7aa25131a08736eee7a42c515c7\nparent a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789927353 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789927353 +0000\n\nRemove the domain timeline chart\n\nThe Gantt band chart restated what the experience timeline and the Work\nsection already say, and its short bands needed a minimum width to stay\nvisible, which distorted the very thing it was drawing.\n\n\"By the numbers\" keeps the stat tiles and the technology-depth bars.\nDropped the chart markup, its CSS, and the ''.gantt'' half of the chart\ndraw-in selector rather than leaving them unreferenced.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px in both themes and with JavaScript\ndisabled: no horizontal overflow, no page errors, bars still draw in.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAD2Ekp9\nUD9rKjB1v8aCrc8muEzeZZjcLj45PS0fFlf28WM0BvSh1RSTxytX5FwXoHKQIE0zh55UISVeyfhm\noQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T18:02:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/de0ed910830ce7288c816d9267f8fa2f3466f6a5","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKGRlMGVkOTEwODMwY2U3Mjg4YzgxNmQ5MjY3ZjhmYTJmMzQ2NmY2YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2","sha":"a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2"}],"sha":"de0ed910830ce7288c816d9267f8fa2f3466f6a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/de0ed910830ce7288c816d9267f8fa2f3466f6a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T17:52:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T17:52:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add data sections, an architecture diagram and a motion layer\n\nThe page read as a wall of cards. It now carries figures and two\ndrawings that say something prose can''t, plus motion that reacts to\nreading rather than decorating.\n\nNew \"By the numbers\" section, every figure computed from the dated\nproject history in the CV rather than estimated:\n- Four stat tiles (84 months of .NET, 15 projects, largest team of 12,\n  9 domains), counting up when scrolled into view.\n- A domain timeline: nine bands drawn across the months each domain ran,\n  so overlapping work is visible instead of implied.\n- Technology depth: months of project time per technology, top ten.\n\nNew \"How I build\" section: a hand-authored inline SVG of the system\nshape most of this work lands on — clients through a gateway to .NET\nservices, a queue feeding background workers, a shared data layer, and\nthe pipeline that deploys it. Every arrow is labelled; the caption\nstates why the queue is the piece worth drawing.\n\nCharts follow one-series-one-hue, with the value printed beside every\nbar so nothing is encoded in colour alone. The series colour was checked\nagainst both surfaces with the palette validator (>= 3:1 both modes).\n\nMotion: scroll-progress bar, drifting hero grid and orbs, rotating role\ntext, a tech marquee, cursor spotlight on cards, pointer tilt on the\ncode card, and draw-in for the bars and timeline dots.\n\nRobustness, since these sections hide data behind state:\n- Collapsed bar states are scoped to a `js` class set in the head, so\n  with JavaScript off every chart renders at full length.\n- Counters are zeroed inside the observer callback rather than upfront,\n  so an element whose observer never fires keeps its real value.\n- prefers-reduced-motion disables every animation and transition and\n  renders the charts and counters at their final state.\n\nAlso: nine domain cards (Blockchain added) so the Work section, the\ntimeline and the domain count agree; README gains the same figures.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion contexts: no horizontal overflow, no page errors,\ncounters and charts land on their real values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"c7a64b9453b5f787759a6672b8fb97aefced6403","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/c7a64b9453b5f787759a6672b8fb97aefced6403"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2","verification":{"payload":"tree c7a64b9453b5f787759a6672b8fb97aefced6403\nparent 32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789926737 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789926737 +0000\n\nAdd data sections, an architecture diagram and a motion layer\n\nThe page read as a wall of cards. It now carries figures and two\ndrawings that say something prose can''t, plus motion that reacts to\nreading rather than decorating.\n\nNew \"By the numbers\" section, every figure computed from the dated\nproject history in the CV rather than estimated:\n- Four stat tiles (84 months of .NET, 15 projects, largest team of 12,\n  9 domains), counting up when scrolled into view.\n- A domain timeline: nine bands drawn across the months each domain ran,\n  so overlapping work is visible instead of implied.\n- Technology depth: months of project time per technology, top ten.\n\nNew \"How I build\" section: a hand-authored inline SVG of the system\nshape most of this work lands on — clients through a gateway to .NET\nservices, a queue feeding background workers, a shared data layer, and\nthe pipeline that deploys it. Every arrow is labelled; the caption\nstates why the queue is the piece worth drawing.\n\nCharts follow one-series-one-hue, with the value printed beside every\nbar so nothing is encoded in colour alone. The series colour was checked\nagainst both surfaces with the palette validator (>= 3:1 both modes).\n\nMotion: scroll-progress bar, drifting hero grid and orbs, rotating role\ntext, a tech marquee, cursor spotlight on cards, pointer tilt on the\ncode card, and draw-in for the bars and timeline dots.\n\nRobustness, since these sections hide data behind state:\n- Collapsed bar states are scoped to a `js` class set in the head, so\n  with JavaScript off every chart renders at full length.\n- Counters are zeroed inside the observer callback rather than upfront,\n  so an element whose observer never fires keeps its real value.\n- prefers-reduced-motion disables every animation and transition and\n  renders the charts and counters at their final state.\n\nAlso: nine domain cards (Blockchain added) so the Work section, the\ntimeline and the domain count agree; README gains the same figures.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px, both themes, plus JS-disabled and\nreduced-motion contexts: no horizontal overflow, no page errors,\ncounters and charts land on their real values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDbf5hQ8\nQkKitQsG8p68EzoiPjtLUE54dqyyRw6jnFI2Xx2iUVkRW4/c6pV1MtwA0yDLX2tNx1nUZEHr8m/0\nUAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T17:52:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2","node_id":"C_kwDOOcmjE9oAKGE4OTNlOTFiNzJjYjE2ZDdmNGVjYzEwNmFhNzQ5MDg5ZjhhMzkxYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commit/32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a","sha":"32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a"}],"sha":"a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/a893e91b72cb16d7f4ecc106aa749089f8a391c2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/commits/32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T17:24:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T17:24:39Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Replace detailed project list with domain summaries\n\nListing per-project task breakdowns, product names, client identifiers\nand team sizes on a public page is more disclosure than client work\nunder NDA allows. The section now conveys the same range without it.\n\n- Projects section becomes Work (#work, nav label \"Work\"): eight domain\n  cards carrying only domain, period, one sentence and the stack. Drops\n  the per-project bullet breakdowns, the \"Earlier projects\" list and the\n  domain filter chips, which have nothing left to filter.\n- Experience timeline entries keep company, role and technologies; the\n  per-product sentences are generalised to the domains worked in.\n- About paragraph no longer names a client or a team size.\n- README: the selected-projects table becomes a domains table, and the\n  experience table is generalised the same way.\n- Removed the CSS and JS the old section owned (.project*, .filters,\n  .more, the filter handler) rather than leaving them unreferenced.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px in both themes: no horizontal\noverflow, no page errors, scroll spy tracks the renamed #work anchor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019MQ9owEGMgKkCmFVohYkwc","tree":{"sha":"8feaa87f40ffb60103fcd3eac5db64f63c771c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/trees/8feaa87f40ffb60103fcd3eac5db64f63c771c76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/phuongfullstack/phuongfullstack.github.io/git/commits/32165424c5d230088c6100e3f53e6a978f4d6b9a","verification":{"payload":"tree 8feaa87f40ffb60103fcd3eac5db64f63c771c76\nparent ce31f2cc7390c332f536afbd9ed65910f340b366\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789925079 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789925079 +0000\n\nReplace detailed project list with domain summaries\n\nListing per-project task breakdowns, product names, client identifiers\nand team sizes on a public page is more disclosure than client work\nunder NDA allows. The section now conveys the same range without it.\n\n- Projects section becomes Work (#work, nav label \"Work\"): eight domain\n  cards carrying only domain, period, one sentence and the stack. Drops\n  the per-project bullet breakdowns, the \"Earlier projects\" list and the\n  domain filter chips, which have nothing left to filter.\n- Experience timeline entries keep company, role and technologies; the\n  per-product sentences are generalised to the domains worked in.\n- About paragraph no longer names a client or a team size.\n- README: the selected-projects table becomes a domains table, and the\n  experience table is generalised the same way.\n- Removed the CSS and JS the old section owned (.project*, .filters,\n  .more, the filter handler) rather than leaving them unreferenced.\n\nVerified in Chromium at 1440/390px in both themes: no horizontal\noverflow, no page errors, scroll spy tracks the renamed #work anchor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthrop