er}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berfinyuksel/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/berfinyuksel","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commits/dd5ce13da131a3671008f5ff6ba2247f16aebab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:00:05Z","email":"99557970+berfinyuksel@users.noreply.github.com","name":"berfinyuksel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:00:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pass SYNC_TOKEN to the studio frontend build (#43)\n\nPart of pimcore/DevOps-Tasks#65. The studio frontend build pushes its automatic commits as pimcore-deployments and only on pushes to version branches; PR runs upload the build as an artifact instead (pimcore/workflows-collection-public#168). The push run no longer cancels an in-progress run; the head-commit check in the reusable prevents a commit loop.\n\nUntil #168 is merged the \"Studio Frontend Build\" check fails at startup with \"secret SYNC_TOKEN is not defined in the referenced workflow\". That is expected; the check gets re-run after the merge, before this PR is marked ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d1bc0742f13d20792c2ecf895ad15c3f771e1995","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/git/trees/d1bc0742f13d20792c2ecf895ad15c3f771e1995"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/git/commits/dd5ce13da131a3671008f5ff6ba2247f16aebab0","verification":{"payload":"tree d1bc0742f13d20792c2ecf895ad15c3f771e1995\nparent e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477\nauthor berfinyuksel <99557970+berfinyuksel@users.noreply.github.com> 1791396005 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791396005 +0200\n\nPass SYNC_TOKEN to the studio frontend build (#43)\n\nPart of pimcore/DevOps-Tasks#65. The studio frontend build pushes its automatic commits as pimcore-deployments and only on pushes to version branches; PR runs upload the build as an artifact instead (pimcore/workflows-collection-public#168). The push run no longer cancels an in-progress run; the head-commit check in the reusable prevents a commit loop.\n\nUntil #168 is merged the \"Studio Frontend Build\" check fails at startup with \"secret SYNC_TOKEN is not defined in the referenced workflow\". That is expected; the check gets re-run after the merge, before this PR is marked ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxoilCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFeQQAIU2NXIOHDI/WGquo0EatZDG\n33S6x2S7rs5pUngehpWB3IICYYqkQHrK1zWaA6DFlX/QPhUJ6JZFKgk6vmnFWN26\nbr2mA4sEfDBuX2+CBcaEo6Lx3CW7qFZNBU4sXiNfY/vNwngQoVK+tr7kTqhgZWUa\nII7R+I3kOkBs/y+FnkRNDcwmoa8nC1fg566pyKo99wyeZa6oENF57XuQx15Kzh/L\n9c4wSUKrWtAISv/+ENtT/lZdauUUpHVf5dumxj/ygcd3qadgluyw6PIEz37AennK\n3taa0tLlt8EqCTEgVJKuKyG/fMXo6ZN3Pt7XCXbObuiq4oHWzOmybZVCHGZp0rVW\nKFH2DKW1g+H726JFp8qimX1zoX1UJyA3oD4aDId5IOH7Ae3ehJa5i7a/XVW5Ce+7\nlnlIVh8X5WE8sqn1Zg3COrGs+AfPLw1XXR/7/SxbYnmG4bxeN2Cib2kXE6xgOoqG\n//Pz5lFj1+nJz//bZST5oxBuGFojF0zQ5Uu8C/5q3YN9qS4TgqxKCGvVgT8AYNjY\nU/RvS1gyKzhfAB4eMBkQ4F35uwlRoZR+Tf1QMfNAAhUtkhpYttU6pBv1PndrmxIt\nKoVXb80TO3O/caYT+39PeSUdAiiqtLfk5A+oqQikAHOqWmOs2Y/+ap+HrAauO1m7\n+M4DmEjjiIxBRUzx3SNM\n=wGz4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T18:00:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commit/dd5ce13da131a3671008f5ff6ba2247f16aebab0","node_id":"C_kwDOOdu_dNoAKGRkNWNlMTNkYTEzMWEzNjcxMDA4ZjVmZjZiYTIyNDdmMTZhZWJhYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commit/e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477","sha":"e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commits/e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477"}],"sha":"dd5ce13da131a3671008f5ff6ba2247f16aebab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commits/dd5ce13da131a3671008f5ff6ba2247f16aebab0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11871778?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ValeriaMaltseva","id":11871778,"login":"ValeriaMaltseva","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODcxNzc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ValeriaMaltseva","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/commits/e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:31:41Z","email":"valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com","name":"Valeriia Maltseva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T15:31:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Ship the frontend build as a packaged archive (#40)\n\n* Ship the frontend build as a packaged archive\n\nReplace the committed public/build/ directory with a single committed\narchive, build-dist/build-<id>.zip, which the Studio UI Bundle extracts\ninto public/build/ during cache warmup.\n\n- rsbuild.config.ts derives the build id from the contents of assets/\n  via getBuildGroupId() instead of a random uuid, and writes it into the\n  output with pluginWriteBuildId(). Unchanged source now yields the same\n  id, so a rebuild produces no diff.\n- Add the package-build script (studio-package-build) and drop the now\n  unused uuid dependency.\n- WebpackEntryPointProvider implements BuildArchiveProviderInterface via\n  BuildArchiveExtractionTrait.\n- Gitignore public/build/ and commit build-dist/ instead.\n- Collapse the two build workflows that were both active into a single\n  thin caller of reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml. The old\n  hand-rolled workflow committed the expanded ./public/ output, and the\n  parked reusable caller watched assets/studio/** which does not exist\n  in this repo.\n\nThe archive mechanism needs studio-ui-bundle 2025.4.9+ or 2026.2.1+, so\nthe composer constraint and the npm dependency are raised accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Keep studio-frontend-build.yaml untouched, update the .yml caller instead\n\nRestore .github/workflows/studio-frontend-build.yaml to its state on main\nand move the packaged build over to studio-frontend-build.yml, which now\ncalls reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml with\nworking-directory: assets and watches assets/** instead of the\nassets/studio/** path that does not exist in this repository.\n\nRenamed to \"Studio Frontend Build Packaged\" so the two workflows are\ndistinguishable in the Actions UI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clean up comments in studio-frontend-build.yml\n\nRemoved comments explaining the build process.\n\n* Keep public/build/ in git and drop the added peer markers from the lock\n\nGitignoring the expanded build left no tracked file under public/, so the\ndirectory would not exist after a fresh composer install and there would\nbe nothing for assets:install to link. Track public/build/.gitkeep and\nnegate it in .gitignore, following studio-ui-bundle.\n\nThe pre-build cleanup in rsbuild.config.ts swept every entry in\npublic/build/, which deleted that .gitkeep on each build. Restrict it to\ndirectories; plain files at that level are left alone. pluginWriteBuildId\nalready skips non-directories.\n\nRemove the 43 \"peer\": true markers that the dependency update added to\nassets/package-lock.json, keeping the 2 that were already there. They are\ninstall metadata and do not affect npm ci resolution.\n\nThe build id is a hash of assets/, so the lockfile and config edits change\nit: the archive is rebuilt as build-fc755267691a.zip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the superseded inline Studio Frontend Build workflow\n\nstudio-frontend-build.yaml was the old inline lint/check-types/build\npipeline. It was superseded by studio-frontend-build.yml, which delegates\nto the reusable workflow, but the file was never removed, so both ran\nunder the same name \"Studio Frontend Build\".\n\nThe leftover one could not work any more: its jobs inherit the\nworkflow-level `contents: read` permission, so the install job''s\nactions/cache step runs in read mode (\"cache write denied: token has no\nwritable scopes\") and never saves ./assets/node_modules. The dependent\nlint and check-types jobs then start on a cache miss with no\nnode_modules, which is why lint reports \"eslint: not found\" and\ncheck-types falls through to the runner''s global tsc (a newer major that\nremoved baseUrl) without @types/webpack-env installed.\n\nIt also used pull_request_target while checking out the pull request\nhead, which runs fork code with a write-scoped token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Move the lint and check-types jobs into the packaged build workflow\n\nCarries the two jobs over from the removed studio-frontend-build.yaml so\nthe repository keeps its own lint-fix and type-check steps, and turns the\nreusable workflow''s equivalents off so neither runs twice and only one\njob pushes to the branch.\n\nThe jobs install their own dependencies instead of depending on a shared\ninstall job that caches ./assets/node_modules. That cache was the reason\nboth jobs failed: the cache token is not writable here, so the save was\ndenied and the restore missed, leaving the jobs with nothing installed.\nsetup-node''s npm cache is kept, since it caches the download cache rather\nthan the installed tree and needs no cross-job save.\n\nThe build is ordered after both jobs, matching the removed workflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Let the reusable workflow run lint and check-types\n\nThe caller''s own lint and check-types jobs ran npm ci and repo scripts\nwith a contents: write token and persisted git credentials, so any npm\ninstall hook could push to the repository. The reusable packaged workflow\nalready runs the same lint-fix and check-types scripts, but in read-only\njobs without git credentials, and keeps the write token in commit jobs\nthat execute no project code. It also checks out fork PRs via\nrefs/pull/<n>/head, which works for private forks.\n\nDrop the duplicated jobs and go back to a thin caller.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"089a48c7dc554a120c1f3b5eca08c6843e51e1ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/git/trees/089a48c7dc554a120c1f3b5eca08c6843e51e1ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/studio-example-bundle/git/commits/e7738fdde4c9ea81d263f20f7aabbb0412e1c477","verification":{"payload":"tree 089a48c7dc554a120c1f3b5eca08c6843e51e1ca\nparent 8a83ed2010976f6d0e0965b21cdae2d0e0401513\nauthor Valeriia Maltseva <valeriia.maltseva@pimcore.com> 1790782301 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790782301 +0200\n\nShip the frontend build as a packaged archive (#40)\n\n* Ship the frontend build as a packaged archive\n\nReplace the committed public/build/ directory with a single committed\narchive, build-dist/build-<id>.zip, which the Studio UI Bundle extracts\ninto public/build/ during cache warmup.\n\n- rsbuild.config.ts derives the build id from the contents of assets/\n  via getBuildGroupId() instead of a random uuid, and writes it into the\n  output with pluginWriteBuildId(). Unchanged source now yields the same\n  id, so a rebuild produces no diff.\n- Add the package-build script (studio-package-build) and drop the now\n  unused uuid dependency.\n- WebpackEntryPointProvider implements BuildArchiveProviderInterface via\n  BuildArchiveExtractionTrait.\n- Gitignore public/build/ and commit build-dist/ instead.\n- Collapse the two build workflows that were both active into a single\n  thin caller of reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml. The old\n  hand-rolled workflow committed the expanded ./public/ output, and the\n  parked reusable caller watched assets/studio/** which does not exist\n  in this repo.\n\nThe archive mechanism needs studio-ui-bundle 2025.4.9+ or 2026.2.1+, so\nthe composer constraint and the npm dependency are raised accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Keep studio-frontend-build.yaml untouched, update the .yml caller instead\n\nRestore .github/workflows/studio-frontend-build.yaml to its state on main\nand move the packaged build over to studio-frontend-build.yml, which now\ncalls reusable-studio-frontend-build-packaged.yaml with\nworking-directory: assets and watches assets/** instead of the\nassets/studio/** path that does not exist in this repository.\n\nRenamed to \"Studio Frontend Build Packaged\" so the two workflows are\ndistinguishable in the Actions UI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clean up comments in studio-frontend-build.yml\n\nRemoved comments explaining the build process.\n\n* Keep public/build/ in git and drop the added peer markers from the lock\n\nGitignoring the expanded build left no tracked file under public/, so the\ndirectory would not exist after a fresh composer install and there would\nbe nothing for assets:install to link. Track public/build/.gitkeep and\nnegate it in .gitignore, following studio-ui-bundle.\n\nThe pre-build cleanup in rsbuild.config.ts swept every entry in\npublic/build/, which deleted that .gitkeep on each build. Restrict it to\ndirectories; plain files at that level are left alone. pluginWriteBuildId\nalready skips non-directories.\n\nRemove the 43 \"peer\": true markers that the dependency update added to\nassets/package-lock.json, keeping the 2 that were already there. They are\ninstall metadata and do not affect npm ci resolution.\n\nThe build id is a hash of assets/, so the lockfile and config edits change\nit: the archive is rebuilt as build-fc755267691a.zip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop the superseded inline Studio Frontend Build workflow\n\nstudio-frontend-build.yaml was the old inline lint/check-types/build\npipeline. It was superseded by studio-frontend-build.yml, which delegates\nto the reusable workflow, but the file was never removed, so both ran\nunder the same name \"Studio Frontend Build\".\n\nThe leftover one could not work any more: its jobs inherit the\nworkflow-level `contents: read` permission, so the install job''s\nactions/cache step runs in read mode (\"cache write denied: token has no\nwritable scopes\") and never saves ./assets/node_modules. The dependent\nlint and check-types jobs then start on a cache miss with no\nnode_modules, which is why lint reports \"eslint: not found\" and\ncheck-types falls through to the runner''s global tsc (a newer major that\nremoved baseUrl) without @types/webpack-env installed.\n\nIt also used pull_request_target while checking out the pull request\nhead, which runs fork code with a write-scoped token.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Move the lint and check-types jobs into the packaged build workflow\n\nCarries the two jobs over from the removed studio-frontend-build.yaml so\nthe repository keeps its own lint-fix and type-check steps, and turns the\nreusable workflow''s equivalents off so neither runs twice and only one\njob pushes to the branch.\n\nThe jobs install their own dependencies instead of depending on a shared\ninstall job that caches ./assets/node_modules. That cache was the reason\nboth jobs failed: the cache token is not writable here, so the save was\ndenied and the restore missed, leaving the jobs with nothing installed.\nsetup-node''s npm cache is kept, since it caches the download cache rather\nthan the installed tree and needs no cross-job save.\n\nThe build is ordered after both jobs, matching the removed workflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Let the reusable workflow run lint and check-types\n\nThe caller''s own lint and check-types jobs ran npm ci and repo scripts\nwith a contents: write token and persisted git credentials, so any npm\ninstall hook could push to the repository. The reusable packaged workflow\nalready runs the same lint-fix and check-types scripts, but in read-only\njobs without git credentials, and keeps the write token in commit jobs\nthat execute no project code. It also checks out fork PRs via\nrefs/pull/<n>/head, which works for private forks.\n\nDrop the duplicated jobs and go back to a thin caller.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvStdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABxwQABoQ3q+R2M6MJ3HNS73BCHHY\nk6ZcA37vijoFNfQt/DNDyND5b4OOpLWiuYkDKQcHN5kb5vTvfq1l9Ko2GC8c7lBe\nUu92FzA/O8gneIQFEKyKHiXWXaY3Mrw3lCKDeR3Kkwxol8IM0T1NyIkmCe1CgpcU\ne1et2KlS77DTxpTA9aP4f1jU3tOzz41+QKWWaWr3yFtgn1kDfcGEw/jNrzxtEvwX\nuZnZ+LZIaWENkYy/46v8TQYR5rYnr/innJ1ge7+1BqAnhxSgIVMaA5ngdZSTMY4d\nRkGlzCCI3VoAdtN9cBtqzDbAJL91VhNCzB1auDqJUrSN5EEs/6dh/eADlR3GxneT\nBKpqlQHrJH9YvMZI0vnyt3ksW0xvpBJZtJLIWO4Tgd+6uMS3DHKZySyyhL5DYqYH\ndhyXr0eLEMcWLbFEIdYQaPDh+urOpdW139PAHDrMVKNkBgmpta9kzAkEg19pe+Jp\nZ5mcJZhaYSkN6dWs1z4jw8Qrj/5ZYEN5wxidYUkqbtzYd+5+5vsNVIWVeTE9lWaQ\nF6iHhgCN4KpGON9WrwS3K5Dhczb5cZQeXaQqnj1bd471eHTAgMXpv9JSSZkLAphJ\nGQAovtM5/abupRsU/vAEhGqDarHECExVcCL7vKuKHdJMSagaKZb0J1oaCyWTZQQ1\n5IeCpYQqGQpnh6QobzIA\n=S6fg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T15:31:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/use